===Notable MPs===
*Following the retirement of Peter Dunne, National leader [[Bill English]] (list) became the new [[Father of the House (New Zealand)|Father of the House]], having served as an MP continuously since 1990.
*23-year-old [[Chlöe Swarbrick]] (Green, list) became the new [[Baby of the House#New Zealand|Baby of the House]]. She is the youngest MP to be elected to Parliament since 1975.<ref>{{cite web |first= brad |last= Flahive |date= 23 September 2017 |title= Chloe Swarbrick set to become New Zealand's youngest MP in 42 years |url= https://www.stuff.co.nz/national/politics/97175081/new-zealands-youngest-mp-in-42-years |publisher=Stuff.co.nz}}</ref>

==Demographics==
===Gender representation===
Of the 120 MPs elected, 46 are women ({{Percentage|46|120|0}}). This is the highest number since women were first allowed to stand for Parliament in {{NZ election link year|1919}}.<ref name="women">{{cite web |title=Record number of women MPs in New Zealand Parliament |url=https://www.parliament.nz/en/get-involved/features/record-number-of-women-in-new-zealand-parliament/ |publisher=New Zealand Parliament |accessdate=27 June 2019 |language=en |date=8 March 2018}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |title=Record level of women in New Zealand Parliament |url=https://www.newshub.co.nz/home/politics/2017/11/record-levels-of-women-in-new-zealand-parliament.html |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20171107073029/http://www.newshub.co.nz/home/politics/2017/11/record-levels-of-women-in-new-zealand-parliament.html |url-status=dead |archive-date=7 November 2017 |accessdate=27 June 2019 |work=[[Newshub]] |date=11 July 2017 |language=en}}</ref>  The previous record was in [[2008 New Zealand general election|2008]], when 41 female MPs were elected.<ref name="women"/>

